  "body": "## What happens\n\nPR #4492 (UI plan P, #4483) shows the safety state on the folded Browser and Properties chips as text with a glyph. The independent pre-review of head `1bca29cc9` found four small points:\n\n1. In `fold_chip` (`crates/ui-kit/src/fold.rs`), `let _ = turned(...)` drops the state text without a word when the pane is too short for it. The tooltip still carries the state, but the chip then shows nothing. Paint the glyph alone when the text does not fit, so the chip never looks \"clean\" by accident.\n2. The \"Blocked\" and \"Not generated\" paths of both chips have no test. Only \"Up to date\" and the stale path are pinned.\n3. Per-operation warnings (for example \"4 warnings\" on an operation that is up to date) are not on the chip. Add a short warnings count to the Browser chip, or say in the decision file why not.\n4. A folded leaf with several tabs shows the state only for its active tab. Say so in the decision file, or show the state of the tab that holds the Browser or Properties pane.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test for each of points 1 and 2 (a short pane shows the glyph; a blocked and a never-generated operation show on both chips).\n- Point 3 and 4: done, or a line in `docs/decisions/4483-pane-fold.md`.\n- No change to toolpaths, posts or the project file.\n\nAfter #4492 merges.\n",
